&lt;p class=&quot;s25&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Sony Music Publishing is separate from Sony Music&#39;s recorded music business. While Sony Music signs and develops recording artists, Sony Music Publishing signs and represents songwriters and composers, helping maximise the value and use of their compositions. This is the first year with SMP internship opportunities in our programme and we are very excited to be able to offer you the chance to join the Publishing team!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;s25&quot;&gt;The Data Analytics Intern at Sony Music Publishing (SMP) will work within the A&amp;amp;R Research team which sits inside the UK A&amp;amp;R team. The A&amp;amp;R Research team are responsible for being the wider A&amp;amp;R teams eyes and ears online - leveraging data to give them visibility into the market. Which artists, songs and songwriters are having success today and who are the stars of tomorrow. Using data, the A&amp;amp;R Research team assist with discovery as well as quantifying talent and songs across DSPs, social, radio and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;s25&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note: This application form cannot be saved part-way through. We recommend preparing your answers in a separate document and then copying them into the form when you’re ready to submit. If you’d like to take additional time to complete your application, please ensure you gather your responses externally before submitting in one go.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;s25&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you have any reasonable adjustment requests, please reach out to -----
