&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Office attendance: Monday to Thursday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offsite working: No offsite working required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discover and track growing songs and writers for the team, explore what is causing the growth and the story behind the data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research available writers and maintain internal records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new methods and metrics to draw insights from existing data sources and investigate emerging data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on coding projects to analyse and ingest data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, execute, and present analytical projects that build the team’s understanding of music trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with administrative needs such as documentation and manual database updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and quantitative skills, demonstrated through a degree in a quantitative discipline (e.g. Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Computer Science or Economics) or through equivalent practical experience, personal projects, competitions, or self-directed learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beginner to intermediate in Python and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide answers to loosely defined questions and provide actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, comfortable relaying insights to both technical and non-technical audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL and/or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Statistical modelling experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Music fan and knowledge of the modern music landscape, familiarity with music data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
